  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperation framework for Saudi Arabia-Preparatory assistance for the programming phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Saudi economy is the largest in the Middle East and the 18th-largest in the world. The national authorities guided by the Saudi Vison 2030 have opted for the diversification of Saudi Arabia#s economy and develop innovative industrial and service sectors  . Though currently dominated by oil, but the long-term diversification plan, Vision 2030, aims to present substantial opportunities for local and foreign investors and entrepreneurs. Diversifying the economy to nurture entrepreneurship, innovation and entering into global and regional value chains is a strategic priority of the Government. This can be achieved through a structural transformation of the industrial sector, covering many areas including skills development, localization, entrepreneurship development, innovation, research, and investment promotion. Followed by UNIDO Director General&apos;s visit to Saudi Arabia in January 2023, consultations between UNIDO and the Ministry of Industry and Mineral Resources (MIM) have been ongoing on various avenues of cooperation including formulation of a Cooperation Framework (CF). The Saudi high-level delegation representing the Ministry (MIM) during its visit to UNIDO HQ in March 2023 presented the National Industrial Strategy 2022 (NIS) and engaged in several discussions with UNIDO departments. These continuous c</narrative>
  </description>
